 "notes": "Exclusion limit extracted from Figure 4, red 'PSI-HgM-sideband' curve. 95% CL limit from null result of free-spin precession measurement of 199Hg in 1 \u03bcT magnetic field at PSI. Assumes equal axion-neutron and axion-proton couplings (g_ann=g_app) as stated in paper. Conversion from paper's g_aNn (GeV^-1, non-relativistic form L=g\u2202_\u03bca N\u0304\u03b3^\u03bc\u03b3_5 N) to canonical g_an (dimensionless) using g_an=2m_n g_paper with m_n=0.939 GeV. Search covers axion mass range 10^-16 eV \u2264 m_a \u2264 10^-13 eV (Compton frequencies 0.024-24.2 Hz). Peak sensitivity reported as 3.5\u00d710^-6 GeV^-1. Limit increases above ~30 Hz due to finite axion field coherence time (\u03c4_c\u224813.1 s for stated mass range). Dashed black curve shows expected future sensitivity (improvement factor of 10).",
